Z||000000||JAMIE||04-23-2001||12:37 PM||||A number of forum members have asked if I had spoken to George re this issue.The answer is  "no" - I dealt with Terry as he was the person I dealt with when I bought the covers - to me, the Fiero Shop WAS Terry.If I had known otherwise I may well have talked to George. Terry did say he would speak to George about it in his last email reponse to me about a week ago, which was the first time he informed me that he was "just there helping George and had no liabilty for Fiero Shop activities".Things may well have been different had I known this before now.<P>George, I returned the covers because there were several marks that looked to me like burn marks - the need for a cleaning was not an issue as this could be easily done - the covers were at best 7.5/10 - my existing covers are in better shape.I have been relentlessly gathering parts for 3 years now - for restoration of an 88GT - all parts purchased were either new or 9.5/10 used - if your covers were that good,or even a 9/10 you can be sure I would not have returned them - why would I? You may feel they are mint but I do not share that opinion.<P>Please clarify what you mean when you say I am entitled to a  " store credit " and not a refund.Are you saying that you will not reverse the charge on my card but will allow me to buy $300 worth of other parts from you? If so, we have a problem - the understanding I had with Terry was that I could return them for full refund if I was not satisfied.Think about it - wouldn't it be a little absurd for me to agree to a store credit of $450 Canadian dollars if I was not satisfied - is there any Forum member out there who would agree to this type of arrangement for this much money?<BR>AND - WHY WOULD TERRY SAY ABOVE THAT THE CREDIT CARD MACHINE WAS EXPERIENCING PROBLEMS WHEN HE OFFERED THAT AS A POTENTIAL EXPLANATION FOR THE DELAY IN PROCESSING MY REFUND IF, AS YOU SAY NOW, I WAS ENTITLED TO A STORE CREDIT AND NOT A REFUND. DOESN'T ADD UP DOES IT ? <P>All I want is what I agreed to - my money back. Please tell the Forum members if you will honour this agreement.I am sure they would be interested in your response given many are potential customers.<P>Again, I am really sorry things have gotten to this point but you have really left me no alternative.<P>Jamie<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||04-23-2001||01:13 PM||||Jamie, I will say this one more time -- I do not have responsibility for this shop - now, if that bothers you or anyone else here, I am sorry. All I do is work here (and a lot of time is spent working on my own cars rather than customer cars) - I do appear on here more than George due to the fact that I am a web designer as is my personal business and therefore am on the computer quite a bit.<P>Now, the word "credit" - when I spoke to George I told him to provide a credit against a debit that was made to your card -- debit $300 - credit $300 = $0, right? Now, once again, you are holding <B>me</B> responsible for something that fieroshop (George) posted - I do not control the man nor do I control his words.........and, as was mentioned to you several times - we have a toll free number (which is always posted in my profile info just to the left of this post) which you may avail yourself of to continue the conversation with George Miller dba Fiero Shop...........||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-23-2001||01:23 PM||||If anyone on here is like myself, I don't know. <BR>I don't care how this turns out. You could solve all of this with one simple phone call(canada has phones, right?), in several minutes, max. Instead, you choose to waste bandwidth, use server resorces, cost Cliff more money for space to post this. This is something that should be very easy to clear up with a phone call. I don't know how many times you contacted them about this, sounds like it is news to them, so I assume not many. Most everyone on here has already made their mind about FieroShop, good or bad, and your experience will have little to no affect on their purchasing/labor decisions about the shop. You're trying to get "public leverage" by posting this here. Terry has provided you with a number, why not call and solve this in private???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||04-23-2001||02:16 PM||||People, I'm getting a bit sick and tired that everybody is starting new threads while it's actually a reply to another, <B>active</B> thread. I've asked politely now a few times not to do that - but people seem to choose to totally disregard my request.<P>I haven't read the messages in this thread, but I find it a total waste to start a "Part 2" thread while "Part 1" is still active.||||reg||1
